        {
          "id": 671731192,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "[wireshark-filter ](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/man-pages/wireshark-filter.html): `Wireshark and TShark share a powerful filter engine ...`  \n  \nWhat if the `-z` sections where taken out of the `tshark` and `wireshark` man pages and moved to a new man page?  \nThat would be a single place to maintain changes and could be formatted better, grouping like items.  \n  \n\nMaybe the `-Y` option in the `Wireshark` man page should mention `wireshark-filter(4)` but more important,  \nit's short and sweet with all the detail spelled out over in the `wireshark-filter` man page.  \n\n```\n-Y|--display-filter <displaY filter>\nStart with the given display filter.\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
